<title>ITALY: ALPINE SKIING-ALPHAND WINS BORMIO DOWNHILL.</title>
<headline>ALPINE SKIING-ALPHAND WINS BORMIO DOWNHILL.</headline>
<dateline>BORMIO, Italy 1996-12-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>France's Luc Alphand won a men's Alpine skiing World Cup downhill on Sunday in a time of two minutes 0.51 seconds, according to unofficial results.</p>
<p>Switzerland's William Besse was second in 2:00.72 and Italian Kristian Ghedina third in 2:01.18.</p>
